%% UC-19 — Manage studies, groups, study codes & questionnaire schedule
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor R as Researcher / Admin
    participant AP as Admin Panel
    participant B as Backend (studyService / studyCodeService / questionnaireScheduleService)
    participant M as MongoDB
    participant F as Flutter App (participant device)

    R->>AP: Open Studies page
    AP->>B: GET /api/v1/admin/studies
    B->>M: find(studies, {isActive: true})
    B-->>AP: studies with G1-G4 groups
    R->>AP: Create study / edit groups / set per-group cueConfig / set end date & end-of-study notification content
    AP->>B: POST or PUT /api/v1/admin/studies/:id (groups[].cueConfig, endDate, endOfStudyNotification {title, body})
    B->>M: upsert(studies) - validator enforces group index 1..4
    B-->>AP: 200
    R->>AP: Open Reminders tab; set habit/questionnaire/endOfStudy/studyUpdate mode + time, study-wide and per group
    AP->>B: PUT /api/v1/admin/studies/:id {reminders} and PATCH .../groups/:groupId/config {reminders}
    B->>M: upsert(studies) - reminders resolved per-group-then-study via reminderConfigService
    B-->>AP: 200
    R->>AP: Generate study codes for a group
    AP->>B: POST /api/v1/admin/studies/:id/codes {groupId, maxRedemptions, expiresAt}
    B->>M: insert(study_codes)
    B-->>AP: 201 codes (distributed to participants out-of-band)
    R->>AP: Open Schedule tab; click "Today" or a calendar day to add a questionnaire assignment
    AP->>B: POST /api/v1/admin/studies/:id/questionnaire-assignments {questionnaireId, groupId, cadence}
    B->>M: insert(questionnaire_assignments); regenerate questionnaire_windows for enrolled participants
    B-->>AP: 200 - calendar shows real windows + dashed "projected" preview for not-yet-enrolled scopes
    Note over F,B: On next app open:
    F->>B: GET /api/v1/questionnaires/due
    B-->>F: {reminders (questionnaire mode/time), questionnaires, studyEndDate, endOfStudyNotification (mode/time + title/body)}
    F->>F: Cancel + reschedule local notification for studyEndDate (flutter_local_notifications)
    Note over F: Fires on-device at the resolved mode/time, even offline (skipped entirely if mode is off)
